nd $5$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n0.\\overset{―}{25}=0.2525252525…\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n0.\\overset{―}{25}=\\frac{25}{99}.\n$$\n\n- $7.526380…$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$…$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. However, there are no repeating digits.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408188 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186489169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408188 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186489170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408188 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186489171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408188 #edb/ref 1031 "Rational Numbers as Finite or Repeating Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408188 #edb/ref 1033 7011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408188 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "24a28f9b-1f4f-5349-9353-6e0a556259c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1045 "Rational Numbers as Finite or Repeating Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186489345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186408188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1050 480.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488466 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f5d315b3-1937-521