td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{238}{8}=29.75.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489207 #edb/ref 1071 "Convert $\\frac{74}{5}$ into a decimal using long division." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40ca59d6-4e89-5334-bddb-bed9c8ab1c58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489207 #edb/ref 1074 "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n74÷5\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,1\\,4\\,.\\,8$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{7\\,\\phantom{|}4\\,.\\,0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{74}{5}=14.8.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489222 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489222 #edb/ref 1069 "q-223772" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489222 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489222 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following numbers are rational?\n\nI. $1.353124…$\n\nII. $1.5\\overset{―}{21}$\n\nIII. $4.055$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489222 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f502aa5-65d4-518a-a479-69aa4507aee1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489222 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $1.353124…$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$…$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. However, there are no repeating digits.\n\n- $1.5\\overset{―}{21}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overset{―}{21}$ tells us that the digits $2$ and $1$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n1.5\\overset{―}{21}=1.52121212121…\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n1.5\\overset{―}{21}=\\frac{1\\,506}{990}.\n$$\n\n- $4.055$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n4.055=\\frac{4\\,055}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489227 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489227 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489227 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489227 #edb/ref 1071 "Convert $\\frac{62}{5}$ into a decimal using long division." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489227 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "63a4febd-402b-590e-88f3-6d9132bd98e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489227 #edb/ref 1074 "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n62÷5\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,1\\,2\\,.\\,4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{6\\,\\phantom{|}2\\,.\\,0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{62}{5}=12.4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489245 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22727" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489245 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following numbers are rational?\n\nI. $1.577$\n\nII. $8.163452 \\ldots$\n\nIII. $2.\\overline{73}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489245 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "975545b6-bff4-5fab-aaf4-e8ee01507788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489245 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of our numbers in turn.\n\n- $1.577$ is a rational number because it can be expressed as a ratio of two integers:\n\n$$\n1.577 = \\dfrac{1\\,577}{1\\,000}\n$$\n\n- $8.163452 \\ldots$ is not a rational number. The notation \"$\\ldots$\" tells us that digits after the decimal point extend forever. Because there is no indicated repeating pattern, this represents a non-terminating, non-repeating decimal.\n\n- $2.\\overline{73}$ is a rational number. The notation $\\overline{73}$ tells us that the digits $7$ and $3$ after the decimal point repeat indefinitely.\n\n$$\n2.\\overline{73} = 2.73737373\\ldots\n$$\n\nAny decimal with repeating digits can be represented as a ratio of two integers. In this case,\n\n$$\n2.\\overline{73}  = \\dfrac{271}{99}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489282 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489282 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357506" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489282 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489282 #edb/ref 1071 "Convert $\\frac{35}{6}$ into a repeating decimal using long division." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489282 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7f88181-a4ac-5313-9245-814758011d78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489282 #edb/ref 1074 "To write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n35÷6\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, continuing until a repeating pattern of digits appears after the decimal point:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<br/><br/><table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"6\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\,5\\,.\\,8\\,3\\,3\\,…$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"6\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{3\\,\\phantom{|}5\\,.\\,0\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td><td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-$</td><td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,⋮$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe could continue the division, but the same digit keeps repeating. Thus, the decimal continues with repeating $3$'s:\n\n$$\n5.833…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{6}=5.833…=5.8\\overset{―}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489286 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489286 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357330" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489286 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489286 #edb/ref 1071 "Convert $\\frac{17}{8}$ into a decimal using long division." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489286 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee55fb2d-2168-5fe7-9d4c-8b219d79c6ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489286 #edb/ref 1074 "To write down the given fraction as a decimal, we need to divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n17÷8\n$$\n\nWe proceed using the long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0:$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\,2\\,.\\,1\\,2\\,5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"5\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{1\\,\\phantom{|}7\\,.\\,0\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{17}{8}=2.125.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489298 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489298 #edb/ref 1061 653256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489298 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07766a04-75bc-582b-a3f7-a4d9e94b4bfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489298 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489328 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489328 #edb/ref 1061 653258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489328 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "722917c0-0a2f-564d-92a1-3b8f90e0a367" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489328 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489169 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489335 #edb/ref 1061 653261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489335 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "84e16e8f-676c-575f-83e7-d1a743860017" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489335 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1061 653255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "989620d9-34b2-5998-bf43-7b078a5551e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489343 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1061 653251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9d911030-9a41-5eba-8339-d738949a2899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489345 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1061 653252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dd795099-acd6-53fe-9be5-05e82111a5a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489372 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1061 653257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e016072c-e22d-536a-a6ed-5eef7793da16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489373 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1064 "A rational number can have a decimal representation that either *ends* or *repeats*.\n\nIn this lesson, we will see how to convert rational numbers written as fractions into decimals using *long division*. \nWe begin with examples where the decimal terminates. \n\nLet's convert $\\dfrac{7}{2}$ into a decimal using long division.\n\nTo write the fraction as a decimal, we divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n$$\n7 \\div 2\n$$\n\nWe proceed using long division as usual, stopping once we obtain a remainder of $0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,3    {\\, . \\,} 5$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{7   {\\, . \\,} 0}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{2} = 3.5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1065 15179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "6c539020-aca7-5b8f-a2b0-b72c56336242" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489385 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1064 "The key takeaway for this lesson is that every repeating decimal is rational! In other words, every repeating decimal can be expressed as a ratio of two integers.\n\nFor example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{3} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0.\\overset{―}{78} & =\\frac{26}{33} \\\\ 0.333\\overset{―}{67} & =\\frac{16517}{49500}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn a future lesson, we'll learn how to express a repeating decimal as a fraction. For now, you can verify these results using a calculator." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1065 15181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "77b1162b-17a9-5251-8efe-31b7034274d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489386 #edb/ref 1067 "Any Repeating Decimal is a Rational" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1064 "It's convenient to use the following special **bar-notation** to indicate decimals that repeat indefinitely:\n\n$$\n0.\\overline{3} = 0.333\\,333\\ldots\n$$\n\nSome decimals have two or more digits that repeat indefinitely. For example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{78} & =0.78\\,78\\,78\\,78… \\\\ 0.\\overset{―}{675} & =0.675\\,675\\,675…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSome repeating decimals have non-repeating digits before the repeating part. For example:\n\n$$\n0.45\\overline{67} = 0.45\\,67\\,67\\,67\\,67\\ldots\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1065 15180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "8545445f-23ee-5309-8571-5a1f6a4b253d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489387 #edb/ref 1067 "Notations for Repeating Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the following rational number:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac13\n$$\n\nTo find its decimal representation, we divide $1$ by $3$ using long division, as follows:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"4\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,0 \\,. 3 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 3 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\:\\ldots$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"4\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{1 {\\, . \\,} 0  {\\:\\phantom{|}} 0 {\\:\\phantom{|}} 0}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\!\\!\\!\\!\\!$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$9$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\ldots$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that, in this case,\n\n- the long division process never ends, and\n\n- the digit $3$ after the decimal point repeats *forever*.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac13 = 0.333\\,333\\ldots\n$$\n\nThis is an example of a **repeating decimal** - a decimal in which the digits after the decimal point continue forever in a *repeating pattern*." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1065 15177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b877953a-1821-5fae-aebf-3ff936971679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489388 #edb/ref 1067 "Repeating Decimals" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
